# A keyed read that names every field. Run with
# `kanso play keyed_read_all_fields.kso`.
#
# Expected: `kanso check` refuses it, the way it refuses `_` in a positional
# pattern, since the rule is about how the source is written ("a keyed read
# omits at least one field; reading every field is the positional form").
# Actual: `kanso check` passes on a module holding the same function (it did
# on zola/front.kso), and the program fails when the line runs, with
# error[runtime]: a keyed read omits at least one field; reading every field
# is the positional form -- with no file or line under `kanso play`, and as
# `zola:88:18` (module, not file) under `kanso test`.
type ylevel
  map
  next

fn shown level
  { map next } = level
  "{map} {next}"

print (shown (ylevel {} 3))
